  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Warm and dry conditions this afternoon with\nsunny skies and temps around 80 inland and 70s along the coast.\nA dry back door cold front will push through the region tonight\nbringing a cool down over the weekend with temps dropping to\nnear normal and lows near to slightly above normal over the\nweekend.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...High pres ridge begins to break down by Wednesday\nas an amplified upper trough over the central CONUS approaches\nthe region. The attendant sfc low lifts into the Great Lakes\nlate Wednesday into Thursday with a warm front currently \nprogged to lift across ENC Thursday followed by the trailing \ncold front Thursday night. There is decent spread in QPF amounts\namong the models with this system but blend of models is\ncurrently showing around a quarter to three quarters of an inch,\nwhich won't make much of an impact to ongoing drought conditions\nacross the region.",
